From 40486fea9c5c82959b7ffeec10b65540b5917745 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:00:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 87/98] pco, pvr: make descriptor checks when recording draws
 for texture-free shaders

A versioned shader tested at every invocation whether its uniform
buffers are large enough for the constant offsets it reads (reading the
descriptor and comparing the size) before taking its unchecked copy.
When the shader has no texture or image null tests and the driver can
read its uniform buffer descriptors when a draw is recorded (bindings
that are not update-after-bind or partially bound), pco now records the
checks (pco_desc_check) and reads a single shared register instead; the
driver makes the checks for the descriptors bound at the draw and
uploads the result.

Shaders with texture or image null tests keep testing in the shader:
there NIR folds each access's null test inside the checked copy, which
then just returns zeros, while with a flag the shader can't see through
both full copies stay. A first version that did this too made glmark2's
effect2d fragment shader grow from 72 to 166 instruction groups and 32
to 52 temporaries, and the scene 7-10% slower.

glmark2-es2 through zink, off-screen 800x600, FPS of two runs each,
before -> after: conditionals (fragment steps 5) 531/523 -> 544/550,
function medium 459/430 -> 475/525, loop (uniform) 324/345 -> 354/357,
jellyfish 179/177 -> 191/187, the others unchanged.

CTS: robustness list (4025), uniform buffer sample (4773), 5062 list,
loops/indexing/graphicsfuzz list (6428), compute.pipeline (1235),
dynamic rendering sample (6745): identical to before. glmark2 --validate:
27 pass, 0 fail.
